From c937b8957bff3567ca0ed9b3f1c578d802facb88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:01:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(update): leave a gateway pinned to its own checkout out
 of the pause and restart [daveey]

hermes-hub deferred every core update from 2026-11-11 00:41 to 05:43 UTC (11 runs):
"Update deferred: hermes-gateway-askeve-builder does not support idle pause; restart
that gateway on the installed code when idle". That unit runs through a drop-in whose
ExecStart and PYTHONPATH name ~/.hermes/askeve-runtime/core-<sha>, a core older than
the idle pause, so it answers `unsupported` and a restart only brings it back on its
pin. The pause chose its set by HERMES_HOME alone (#93349), so a profile of this home
on another checkout was treated as running the code being replaced.

_systemd_unit_owned_by_update now also asks which checkout the unit's live gateway
loads (update_receipt._gateway_code_root, the reader the fleet receipt already uses
for its `external` rows). A gateway provably on another checkout is named once and
left alone by all three callers: the pre-swap pause, the drain-then-restart and the
best-effort restart. Unknown is never foreign: an unreadable code root keeps today's
behaviour. _gateway_code_root gains the unit's PYTHONPATH as evidence, ahead of the
interpreter's location, for `python -m hermes_cli.main` from a venv outside any
checkout with no status record yet.

Not covered: launchd jobs and bare `gateway run` processes on another checkout.
---
